/** These settings in this aspect should be fixed
  * prior to running any analysis, so that cached values computed
	* during analyses remain valid.
	* Specifically, the settings in this aspect should be:
  *   (1) Be set before computing attributes of AST nodes.
  *   (2) Not be changed during computation of attributes.
  * This is to allow easier utilization of global program settings
  * without having to create inherited attributes on the root node
  * (Program), which seems likes the more complex alternative.
  * For instance, it seems we would have to create the root node (program)
  * and set fields of the root node before JastAdd computes all of the
  * remaining attributes.
  * This requires more dependencies on JastAdd internals.
  *
  * There are other global variables other than in this file, but they
  * (should probably be) final static fields that are fixed for all executions.
  *
  * A purpose of this file is to easily find all global settings that should
  * be set appropriately before performing analyses.
  * However, the VarFrontend class should probably set these fields to default
  * values for easier usage.
  */
aspect Settings
{
	public static Logger ASTNode.LOG = logutil.LogUtil.getGlobalLogger();
}
